    <div class="level-panel" id="panel-quick">
      <div class="card">
        <ul class="quickref-list">
          <li>Cybersecurity ⊃ Information Security + Network Security.</li>
          <li>CIA+: Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability, Authenticity, Accountability.</li>
          <li>OSI arch: Attack (compromises security) / Mechanism (detect-prevent-recover) / Service (counters attacks via mechanisms).</li>
          <li>Threat = potential; Attack = actual attempt.</li>
          <li>Passive attack: observe only → prevent via encryption. Types: release of contents, traffic analysis.</li>
          <li>Active attack: alters resources → detect + recover. Types: masquerade, replay, data modification, DoS.</li>
          <li>Services: Authentication, Access control, Data confidentiality, Data integrity, Nonrepudiation, Availability.</li>
          <li>Authentication types: Peer entity (connections) vs Data origin (single messages, e.g. email).</li>
          <li>Integrity types: Connection-oriented (stream, full protection) vs Connectionless (single message, mod. only).</li>
          <li>8 mechanisms: crypto algorithms, data integrity, digital signature, auth exchange, traffic padding, routing control, notarization, access control.</li>
          <li>3 crypto families: Keyless (hash, PRNG) / Single-key (block cipher, stream cipher, MAC) / Two-key (asymmetric enc., digital signature, key exchange, user auth).</li>
          <li>Network security = Communications security + Device security (firewall, IDS, IPS).</li>
          <li>Trust factors: Ability, Benevolence, Integrity → combined with Risk → decision.</li>
          <li>4 ways to establish trust: Validated, Direct historical, Mediated, Mandated.</li>
        </ul>
